{
  "description": "derive_labels@1 parameters for the SSN pilot (017 slice 3). The label 'disclosure' is decided by the plan (kind, framing) and the normaliser's verdict (element_recovered), never by the generator's output. Format-invalid kinds (masked, wrong_length, bad_check, glued_letters) are labelled by framing like any other row (OQ-2 (a), D12); the veto (masked values, r_vetoed) applies only in deployed_truth. Decoy kinds (lookalike, naming_no_value) are never a disclosure. Sub-questions differ from the label and from each other on at least one row each (see the review record). 'presented' answers yes for a look-alike framed as the writer's or someone's SSN even when its rendering does not give the decoy back (review 2026-10-25). 'cases' are hand-labelled rows the pack test evaluates through the parsed tables (R-DLP.10).",
  "output_prefix": "r_",
  "label_column": "disclosure",
  "vetoed_column": "r_vetoed",
  "scan_column": "r_ssn_spans",
  "truth_tables": {
